<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech utility CEZ Q1 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Czech utility CEZ Q1 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech electrical utility CEZ a.s. said on Friday that its net profit for the first quarter, calculated according to international accounting standards (IAS), dropped to 2.84 billion crowns from 3.66 billion in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>It added that according to Czech accounting standards, its net profit for the first three months of the year was 2.46 billion crowns compared to 3.51 billion for the same period last year.  </p>
<p>Results for three-month period ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO INTERNATIONAL ACCOUNTING STANDARDS:</p>
<p>(in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit		 2.84     vs     3.66</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	   4.890    vs     6.046</p>
<p> Operating revenues    15.816    vs    16.365</p>
<p> Operating expenses    10.782    vs    10.360</p>
<p> Income tax		 2.050    vs     2.384</p>
<p> Depreciation	     1.629    vs     1.304</p>
<p>Sales of electricity</p>
<p>  and heat		 15.290    vs    15.797</p>
<p>Costs of purchased</p>
<p>  power		     2.313    vs     2.294</p>
<p> Total assets	   162.397    vs   163.478</p>
<p> Basic capital	   59.156    vs    59.156</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO CZECH ACCOUNTING STANDARDS:</p>
<p>(in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit		 2.46     vs     3.51</p>
<p>Total output and</p>
<p>  sales of goods	 15.850    vs    16.411</p>
<p> Operating profit	 5.038    vs     6.090</p>
<p> Total assets	   156.543    vs   158.284</p>
<p> Basic capital	   59.156    vs    59.156</p>
<p> Write-offs		 1.641    vs     1.316</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is CEZ a.s., the country's main electricity generator.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
